ts, so query the by-size buckets rather than","+     * walking the by-offset list up to the limit on every reviewed page. That trades a walk of the","+     * extents in front of the limit for a walk of the buckets large enough to hold the block.","      */","     __wt_spin_lock(session, &block->live_lock);","     limit = block->size - ((block->size / 10) * block->compact_pct_tenths);","     if (offset > limit && !session->compact->dryrun) {","-        el = &block->live.avail;","-        WT_EXT_FOREACH (ext, el->off) {","-            if (ext->off >= limit)","-                break;","-            if (ext->size >= size) {","-                *skipp = false;","-                break;","-            }","-        }","+        if (__wti_block_avail_front_extent(","+              session, block, &block->live.avail, (wt_off_t)size, limit))","+            *skipp = false;","     }","     __wt_spin_unlock(session, &block->live_lock);"," "],"additions":7,"deletions":11,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/third_party/wiredtiger/src/block/block_ext.c","lines":["@@ -138,6 +138,56 @@ __block_size_srch(WT_SIZE **head, wt_off_t size, WT_SIZE ***stack)","             stack[i--] = szp--;"," }"," ","+/*","+ * __wti_block_avail_front_extent --","+ *     Return whether the available list holds an extent of at least \"size\" bytes that starts before","+ *     \"limit\", the point where the region compaction is emptying begins. Only the existence of such","+ *     an extent matters to the caller, so this walks the size-sufficient buckets and returns as","+ *     soon as one of them holds an extent in front of the limit, rather than locating the lowest","+ *     such offset. The list must track sizes, and the caller must hold the live lock.","+ */","+bool","+__wti_block_avail_front_extent(","+  WT_SESSION_IMPL *session, WT_BLOCK *block, WT_EXTLIST *el, wt_off_t size, wt_off_t limit)","+{","+    WT_EXT *ext;","+    WT_SIZE **sstack[WT_SKIP_MAXDEPTH], *szp;","+","+    WT_UNUSED(block);","+","+    /* The live lock must be locked, and the by-size skiplist must be maintained. */","+    WT_ASSERT_SPINLOCK_OWNED(session, &block->live_lock);","+    WT_ASSERT(session, el->track_size != 0);","+","+    /*","+     * The head of the by-offset list is the lowest-offset available extent. If it is already at or","+     * past the limit, nothing in the list starts before the limit, so no extent can qualify.","+     */","+    ext = el->off[0];","+    if (ext == NULL || ext->off >= limit)","+        return (false);","+","+    /* If that same lowest-offset extent is large enough, it is itself the answer. */","+    if (ext->size >= size)","+        return (true);","+","+    /*","+     * Otherwise consult the size buckets. The search positions at the first bucket whose size","+     * satisfies the request, every bucket from there on is size-sufficient, and each bucket's","+     * extents are sorted by offset, so a bucket's head is the lowest offset of that size. An extent","+     * starting at the limit is in the region compaction is emptying rather than in front of it, so","+     * the comparison has to match the one made against the head of the by-offset list above.","+     */","+    __block_size_srch(el->sz, size, sstack);","+    for (szp = *sstack[0]; szp != NULL; szp = szp->next[0]) {","+        ext = szp->off[0];","+        if (ext != NULL && ext->off < limit)","+            return (true);","+    }","+","+    return (false);","+}","+"," /*","  * __block_off_srch_pair --","  *     Search a by-offset skiplist for before/after records of the specified offset.","@@ -979,6 +1029,10 @@ __wti_block_extlist_merge(WT_SESSION_IMPL *session, WT_BLOCK *block, WT_EXTLIST","      * Sometimes the list we are merging is much bigger than the other: if so, swap the lists around","      * to reduce the amount of work we need to do during the merge. The size lists have to match as","      * well, so this is only possible if both lists are tracking sizes, or neither are.","+     *","+     * Th